In article <CHp2Eo.2nG@usenet.ucs.indiana.edu>, thanselm@silver.ucs.indiana.edu (thomas ward hanselman) writes:
|> Here's a more feasible upgrade from the present display used in nethack.
|> Why not write it in 256-color VGA?  It would look a whole lot neater, and 
|> would be easier to write than a 3D version.

256color VGA wouldn't be good because of the decreased resolution.  There is
a program (called chrhack) which will use 8x16 bitmaps instead of normal text
characters.  Includes an editor for the bitmaps.  Requires EGA/VGA.  (EGA
bitmaps are only 8x14)

ftp.uml.edu:/msdos/Games/Utils/chrhac23.zip
wuarchive.wustl.edu:/pub/MSDOS_UPLOADS/games/chrhac23.zip

